schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Seed Phrase (BIP39 / HD Derivation)
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A 12- or 24-word mnemonic, generated per the BIP39 standard from a random
    number and a fixed 2,048-word list, that acts as the master backup for a
    wallet's private keys and addresses across every BIP39-compatible chain
    and wallet app.
  source_traditions:
    - >-
      BIP39 (Bitcoin Improvement Proposal 39) — the cross-wallet standard
      defining the wordlist and phrase-generation/checksum rules.
    - >-
      Hierarchical deterministic (HD) wallet derivation — the design that lets
      one phrase regenerate every private key and address beneath it.
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Used in the article as the foundational self-custody concept: back up the
    phrase once, and it can rebuild every key/address on every chain that
    follows the standard.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - Secret Recovery Phrase (MetaMask's term)
    - mnemonic phrase
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      Seed phrase vs private key vs address: the article is explicit that the
      chain runs phrase -> private keys -> addresses; the phrase is the single
      backup point for all of them, not a stand-in for a private key.
    - >-
      12-word (128-bit entropy) vs 24-word (256-bit entropy) phrases — both
      considered unguessable; 24 words framed as a preference for larger
      treasuries/long-term holdings, not a security requirement.
  tensions:
    - >-
      One phrase controlling many chains is simultaneously the feature (no
      per-chain backups) and the risk (single point of compromise for
      everything at once).
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Treating "seed phrase" as interchangeable with "password" undersells that
    there is no reset mechanism at all — the article stresses this is a
    categorical difference from conventional account recovery.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/seed-phrases.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
